⚠️ PLACEHOLDER — VERIFY BEFORE PUBLISHING ⚠️

This repository is a fork/extension of the original AnswerPool codebase
(https://github.com/AbobakerAhmed/AnswerPool), accompanying the paper
"Your Benchmark Is Not Saturated: Reviving Multiple-Choice Evaluation with
Answer Pooling." A public license file could not be confirmed for that
repository at the time this file was generated.

Before publishing this fork:
  1. Check the original repo's LICENSE file (or lack of one) directly.
  2. If the original has no license, its code defaults to "all rights
     reserved" -- an unlicensed fork republishing that code publicly may
     require the original authors' permission.
  3. If the original has a license (MIT, Apache-2.0, or otherwise), use
     that SAME license here, not a different one, and update the
     copyright line above to credit the original authors alongside any
     new contributions.
  4. Replace [YOUR NAME / ORGANIZATION] above once the correct license
     terms are confirmed.
